<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="59042" href="schedule/2019/spring/ARTD/362/59042.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="ARTD" href="schedule/2019/spring/ARTD.xml">Art--Design</subject><course id="362" href="schedule/2019/spring/ARTD/362.xml">Photography Workshop</course></parents><sectionNumber>T9 </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Topic: SELF AS SUBJECT | Photography as Autobiography. The purpose of this course is not simply to make obviously autobiographical work, per se, but rather to consider your work – which might be documentary, landscape, fashion, or portraiture – through an autobiographical lens. How does (how can) your identity, who you are, influence and inform the images you make?</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ST ">Studio</type><start>09:30 AM</start><end>12:10 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>340</roomNumber><buildingName>Art and Design Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Squier" firstName="J">Squier, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>